# gates/orphan-endpoints.conf — configures gates/check-orphan-endpoints.sh (GATES.md §4, §7).
# Copy this file to gates/orphan-endpoints.conf and keep ONE of the two shapes below.
# Globs are relative to the project root; ** recurses (not into .hidden dirs).
# Full-line "#" comments only: a regex may contain " #". Keys may repeat.
# Check what it extracts with: ./gates/check-orphan-endpoints.sh --list
#
# ---- Shape 1: the product has no routes — say why (printed on every run) ----
# NA: single-user CLI; no network surface
#
# ---- Shape 2: routes and callers ----
# server:  files that DEFINE routes
# route:   regex over each server file; group 1 (or (?P<path>...)) = the path
# client:  files that CALL routes (a server file never counts as a caller)
# exclude: files left out on both sides
# param:   how a parameter is written in a route (optional; the default understands
#          :id {id} <id> <int:id> [id] and *)
#
# Example: Python server (FastAPI / Flask style decorators) + TypeScript client
# server: src/api/**/*.py
# route: @(?:app|router|bp|api)\.(?:get|post|put|patch|delete|route)\(\s*["']([^"']+)["']
# client: web/src/**/*.ts
# client: web/src/**/*.tsx
# exclude: **/*.test.ts
#
# Example: Express (JavaScript / TypeScript)
# server: server/**/*.js
# route: \b(?:app|router)\.(?:get|post|put|patch|delete|all)\(\s*['"`]([^'"`]+)['"`]
#
# Example: Go net/http (1.22+ patterns, method optional)
# server: internal/http/**/*.go
# route: \.HandleFunc\(\s*"(?:(?:GET|POST|PUT|PATCH|DELETE) )?([^"]+)"
